WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.259
Detection engineering is the practice of designing, building, testing, deploying, and maintaining security detections that identify suspicious activity.

2
00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:16.184
A detection is the logic, context, and operational workflow that turns telemetry into a signal defenders can use.

3
00:00:16.184 --> 00:00:19.836
Good detections help teams focus attention where it matters most.

4
00:00:19.836 --> 00:00:31.290
They connect observable behavior to a meaningful question, such as whether an account, workload, host, application, or cloud resource is behaving in a way that deserves investigation.

5
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:35.092
Detection engineering is not measured by the number of alerts generated.

6
00:00:35.092 --> 00:00:43.274
An alert is only useful when it provides enough relevance, context, and confidence for an analyst or automation to make a better decision.

7
00:00:43.274 --> 00:00:47.305
The discipline matters because defenders operate under constraints.

8
00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:59.547
Time, attention, telemetry quality, and business context are limited, so detection work must reduce noise while improving the organizationâ€™s ability to identify suspicious activity.
